Flags: 1 - variate, 
	   2 - variate in transformed form, 
	   3 - calculate from variated parameter 
	   4 - axial (mark valY, means valY=valX)
	   5 - isotropic (mark valY and valZ, means valY=valX and valZ=valX)
Diffusion model index 0: Brownian motion
                      1: Nonbrownian motion
                      2: Anisotropic viscosity
if ipdf=2 then ist=0 and djf is the parallel diffusion coefficient in the director frame 
[djfprp] (1/sec)-perpendicular diffusion coefficient for anisotropic viscosity term
[oss] - Heisenberg spin exchange frequency [oss]
Truncation value for K-space is used if the magnetic tensors in 
the diffusion frame are complex-valued. This can result 
from nonzero alpha or gamma magnetic or diffusion tilt angles.
Truncation value for M-space is used with a nonzero nuclear Zeeman 
Libratrions:
	1 - low angular oscillations around g-axes (as Dzuba);
	   parameters - <sin^2alfa>
	2 - unlimited oscillation around g-axes (analog Griffits) with
       uniform distribution into interval -alfa - +alfa;
	3 - unlimited oscillation around arbitrary axes (analog Timofeev) with
       uniform distribution into interval -alfa - +alfa;
As hw,sdvig and g-values are interconnected values, 
it should be variated at once.
If B0 is indicated, hw is ignored,
if B0=0 , hw used for calculation B0
hw can be variated in transformed form only (2)
NORTANG - number spectra in angular dependence, Names - in name.nam,
          angles psi are taken from first string in each esr spectrum
Lorentz frame itw = 0 - g-frame
                    1 - A-frame
                    2 - diffusion frame